From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luna <luna@localhost>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 13:14:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] x86: call Luna Rust handoff parser from setup

Upstream base: Linux 7.2.4.

Keep the early C side limited to the ABI declaration and invocation.
The setup_arch() path passes only the Linux setup_data head pointer; all
Luna handoff parsing and validation remains in Rust.

Project Luna requires CONFIG_RUST for this kernel profile. Do not silently
continue with the Luna handoff path disabled.

---
 arch/x86/kernel/setup.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c b/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c
@@ -958,5 +958,8 @@ void __init setup_arch(char **cmdline_p)
 	iomem_resource.end = (1ULL << boot_cpu_data.x86_phys_bits) - 1;
 	e820__memory_setup();
 	parse_setup_data();
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_RUST
+	extern void x86_luna_boot_parse(u64 setup_data_phys);
+	x86_luna_boot_parse(boot_params.hdr.setup_data);
+#else
+#error "Project Luna requires CONFIG_RUST"
+#endif
 
 	copy_edd();
